{"skill":{"slug":"video-subtitles","displayName":"Video Subtitles"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769095508613,"changelog":"Initial release: Hebrew/English transcription, translation, burn-in subtitles","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2265,"sha256":"308d80f1bea43b7f1d43f667e7770bd0fa2fd02a8d43a1403cb855899304b0e4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/generate_srt.py","size":11684,"sha256":"0edbed0d2eb8d0c9915f9826dbc859be07927a94293e5579d87d370814867ee1","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1760,"sha256":"ebb2e0ebf2628b675a021b89245c6efd2c32c8fc588dc23ccd04e35cd32411b8","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789016903883,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3a24547065f5cae41a02322208399ddb6afdfa03daa281df71a6f959beaff943","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3a24547065f5cae41a02322208399ddb6afdfa03daa281df71a6f959beaff943","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: video-subtitles\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its use of `subprocess.run` in `scripts/generate_srt.py` to execute the `ffmpeg` command. While this is a legitimate requirement for the stated purpose of burning subtitles into video, `ffmpeg` is a powerful external utility, and the capability to execute arbitrary external commands via `subprocess` always presents a higher risk. Although the script attempts to construct `ffmpeg` arguments carefully and uses an internally generated temporary SRT file, the presence of this high-risk capability without explicit malicious intent warrants a 'suspicious' classification rather than 'benign'.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159835450},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":30,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789016903883},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill appears to do the advertised subtitle work, but it can automatically install changing dependencies and overwrite files without confirmation, so it needs review before use.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Reading media files and producing SRT/MP4 files is proportionate, but the script uses ffmpeg -y, direct output writes, and a predictable /tmp subtitle path, creating avoidable file clobber and local symlink risks.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The uv script auto-resolves faster-whisper with an open-ended version constraint, and the skill notes automatic dependency and model downloads. That is purpose-aligned for transcription, but not pinned or integrity-scoped.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill instructs agents to run a local executable script and write transcript, subtitle, or video outputs, but it does not define narrow tool or path boundaries and the script overwrites outputs without an explicit force option.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No services, startup hooks, memory poisoning, tool replacement, or privilege escalation were found. Runtime dependencies and transcription models may be cached by normal package/model tooling after first use.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is coherent with the artifacts: it transcribes audio or video, generates SRT output, and uses ffmpeg to embed or burn subtitles. I did not find unrelated credential access, exfiltration, prompt hijacking, or destructive behavior outside that workflow.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this before installing. Run it only on media files and output paths you choose, avoid pointing -o at existing important files, and prefer running it in a constrained environment. The publisher should pin dependencies, use secure temporary files, and require an explicit overwrite option.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Local script execution and file output are expected for this media-processing skill, but the lack of explicit tool and path scoping supports a Review concern when combined with overwrite behavior.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The artifact confirms ffmpeg is called with -y and outputs are written directly; generating outputs is expected, but unconditional replacement without a force flag is under-scoped.\n[AST4] expected: The subprocess call invokes ffmpeg using an argument list with shell=False, so the broad command-injection concern is downgraded, though ffmpeg still performs file mutation.\n[T08] unexpected: The transcription dependency is expected, but the open-ended uv dependency resolution is not locked to reviewed versions and can change after review.\n[T09] unexpected: The fixed /tmp/subtitles_temp.srt path is artifact-backed and unnecessary for the purpose; it creates a local symlink and concurrency overwrite risk.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789016903883}}}}}